From 576b83f34734e15086435ae43b63ff85525a1edf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:56:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] meshnet: optional peer_namespace on a link, so a pod can be
 wired to a peer in another namespace

Every peer lookup took the local pod's namespace, so a link could only join
two pods of one topology namespace. A Link may now name peer_namespace; empty
keeps today's behaviour byte-for-byte (same VNI, same veth alias). A
cross-namespace link keys its VNI and veth alias on the ordered namespace
pair, so both ends derive the same wire without coordinating. The remote
Update carries the peer's namespace, skip-list entries for a cross-namespace
peer are ns-qualified, SkipReverse treats a vanished peer Topology as nothing
to record (it failed the DEL), and the grpc inter-node path refuses a
cross-namespace link rather than miswiring it.
